 Advanced PromQL Queries in Prometheus

🔹 What is Advanced PromQL? 🧠
 Advanced PromQL functions help engineers perform calculations, aggregations, and trend analysis on monitoring data.
Instead of viewing raw metrics, you can analyze patterns and system behavior in production 📊

🔹 Why it matters in real-world? 🏗️
 Production systems generate massive amounts of metrics.
 Advanced queries help you:
✔ Detect traffic spikes 🚨
 ✔ Analyze performance trends 📈
 ✔ Calculate averages
 ✔ Build meaningful dashboards

🔹 Important PromQL Functions: ⚡
✔ rate() 🔄
 Calculates how fast a counter increases over time.

👉 Example:
rate(http_requests_total[5m])

✔ Shows request rate per second over 5 minutes
✔ sum() ➕
 Adds values together.

👉 Example:
sum(cpu_usage)

✔ Total CPU usage across systems
✔ avg() 📊
 Calculates average value.

👉 Example:
avg(memory_usage)

✔ Average memory usage across servers

🔹 Real-world Queries: 💡

👉 Total requests from all APIs
sum(http_requests_total)

👉 Average CPU usage of all nodes
avg(node_cpu_usage)

👉 Request rate in last 5 minutes
rate(http_requests_total[5m])

🔹 Real-world Example: 🌍
Your application traffic suddenly increases 📈
👉 rate() shows request spike
 👉 avg() shows high memory usage
 👉 sum() shows total traffic load
✅ Engineers quickly understand system pressure and scale services 🚀

🔹 Key Concepts to Remember: 🧠
✔ rate() = Speed of change 🔄
 ✔ sum() = Total value ➕
 ✔ avg() = Average value 📊
 ✔ Used for dashboards & alerts 🚨
